From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:03:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d: Leave a GL context on the backup DC of a window it
 could not draw to.

When the DC of a context's window cannot be drawn to, typically because
the window is gone, the context falls back to the device's backup window.
The next time it was made current, wined3d_context_gl_update_window() saw
a DC other than the swapchain's and put the dead one back, so every
activation failed once and fell back again.  A context on the backup DC
for the window its swapchain still has now stays there; a new window
still moves it.

Under PowerPoint on GL this leaves one fallback in a run where there were
hundreds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit a3d7408f6b8f2c29d6a872cfd3404e9c23a4799f)

diff --git a/dlls/wined3d/context_gl.c b/dlls/wined3d/context_gl.c
index 58267796d0b..b090e17f5f1 100644
--- a/dlls/wined3d/context_gl.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/context_gl.c
@@ -1300,6 +1300,13 @@ static void wined3d_context_gl_update_window(struct wined3d_context_gl *context_
         context_gl->dc == context_gl->c.swapchain->dc)
         return;
 
+    /* A context on the backup DC for this window is there because the
+     * window's own DC could not be drawn to, typically because the window is
+     * gone; going back to that DC each time the context is made current only
+     * fails again. */
+    if (context_gl->window == context_gl->c.swapchain->win_handle && context_gl->dc_is_private)
+        return;
+
     TRACE("Updating context %p window from %p to %p.\n",
             context_gl, context_gl->window, context_gl->c.swapchain->win_handle);
 
